(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','Attention diners. We are collecting feedback on the new evening menu for the next two weeks. Fill out the card at the cashier or scan the code by the exit, and a sample of responses will be posted on the door with the revised menu.','TTS','["A change in opening hours","A new cashier station","Collecting feedback on the evening menu","A free tasting event"]','C',1,'The notice explains how diners can give feedback on the evening menu.',81),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','Attention diners. We are collecting feedback on the new evening menu for the next two weeks. Fill out the card at the cashier or scan the code by the exit, and a sample of responses will be posted on the door with the revised menu.','TTS','["By card at the cashier or by scanning a code","By emailing the chef","By phoning the office","By writing on the door"]','A',1,'Two routes are offered: the card at the cashier or the code by the exit.',82),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','Attention diners. We are collecting feedback on the new evening menu for the next two weeks. Fill out the card at the cashier or scan the code by the exit, and a sample of responses will be posted on the door with the revised menu.','TTS','["The chef''s photo","The cashier''s schedule","A list of ingredients","A sample of the responses"]','D',1,'A sample of responses will be posted on the door alongside the revised menu.',83),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','Housing notice for Hall C. Room reassignments happen next Friday, so all belongings must be cleared from the hallway by Thursday night. Moving carts can be reserved at the front desk for a two-hour slot, and the elevator on the west side will be out of service that day.','TTS','["Return their key cards","Clear the hallway of belongings","Repaint their rooms","Pay the housing fee"]','B',1,'Belongings must be cleared from the hallway before Friday''s reassignments.',84),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','Housing notice for Hall C. Room reassignments happen next Friday, so all belongings must be cleared from the hallway by Thursday night. Moving carts can be reserved at the front desk for a two-hour slot, and the elevator on the west side will be out of service that day.','TTS','["They are free on the first floor","They are sold at the desk","They are reserved for a two-hour slot","They are forbidden in Hall C"]','C',1,'The notice says carts are reserved at the front desk for a two-hour slot.',85),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','Housing notice for Hall C. Room reassignments happen next Friday, so all belongings must be cleared from the hallway by Thursday night. Moving carts can be reserved at the front desk for a two-hour slot, and the elevator on the west side will be out of service that day.','TTS','["It will be out of service","It will run all weekend","It will be replaced","It stays open late"]','A',1,'The elevator on the west side is unavailable that day.',86),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','A reminder from campus security. After dark, escorts are available by phone and will walk you between buildings and the transit stop. Report a safety concern through the app or at any front desk, and keep your door locked overnight, since most thefts happen through open doors.','TTS','["Free taxi rides","Late-night desk shifts","Guided building tours","Escorts to the transit stop"]','D',1,'The notice says staff will walk people between buildings and the stop after dark.',87),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','A reminder from campus security. After dark, escorts are available by phone and will walk you between buildings and the transit stop. Report a safety concern through the app or at any front desk, and keep your door locked overnight, since most thefts happen through open doors.','TTS','["By calling a neighbour","Through the app or a front desk","By emailing a professor","On the feedback card"]','B',1,'Two channels are named for a concern: the app or any front desk.',88),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_ANNOUNCEMENT','Listen to the announcement and answer the question.','A reminder from campus security. After dark, escorts are available by phone and will walk you between buildings and the transit stop. Report a safety concern through the app or at any front desk, and keep your door locked overnight, since most thefts happen through open doors.','TTS','["Noise carries in","Heat escapes","Most thefts come through open doors","Inspectors check rooms"]','C',1,'The notice links most thefts to doors left open overnight.',89),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_TALK','Listen to the talk and answer the question.','Professor: Today we look at why the first writing was almost boring. The oldest clay tablets from southern Mesopotamia are not poems or prayers; they are tallies of grain, beer, and sheep handed out as rations. A worker received a fixed measure of barley each day, and the temple had to record who took it, or the storehouse would be emptied without a trace. So the earliest signs are numbers, a picture of a stalk, and a mark naming the person. Only later did the wedge-shaped strokes become flexible enough to say more than a receipt. The lesson is that a technology we now link with literature and law grew out of a plain accounting need: keeping track of what was owed to whom. That is why, when you read a ration list, you are seeing the ancestors of the alphabet at their everyday work, pressed into wet clay.','TTS','["The origin of poetry on clay tablets","How record-keepers tracked grain rations","The daily diet of temple workers","The trade routes for barley"]','B',1,'The talk explains that early tablets recorded grain and beer rations, an accounting need.',90),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_TALK','Listen to the talk and answer the question.','Professor: Today we look at why the first writing was almost boring. The oldest clay tablets from southern Mesopotamia are not poems or prayers; they are tallies of grain, beer, and sheep handed out as rations. A worker received a fixed measure of barley each day, and the temple had to record who took it, or the storehouse would be emptied without a trace. So the earliest signs are numbers, a picture of a stalk, and a mark naming the person. Only later did the wedge-shaped strokes become flexible enough to say more than a receipt. The lesson is that a technology we now link with literature and law grew out of a plain accounting need: keeping track of what was owed to whom. That is why, when you read a ration list, you are seeing the ancestors of the alphabet at their everyday work, pressed into wet clay.','TTS','["To show it was too complex","To suggest scribes were poorly trained","To prove writing came from Egypt","To stress that it began as practical record-keeping"]','D',1,'Calling the writing boring and its signs simple underlines that it arose from a practical accounting need.',91),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_TALK','Listen to the talk and answer the question.','Professor: Today we look at why the first writing was almost boring. The oldest clay tablets from southern Mesopotamia are not poems or prayers; they are tallies of grain, beer, and sheep handed out as rations. A worker received a fixed measure of barley each day, and the temple had to record who took it, or the storehouse would be emptied without a trace. So the earliest signs are numbers, a picture of a stalk, and a mark naming the person. Only later did the wedge-shaped strokes become flexible enough to say more than a receipt. The lesson is that a technology we now link with literature and law grew out of a plain accounting need: keeping track of what was owed to whom. That is why, when you read a ration list, you are seeing the ancestors of the alphabet at their everyday work, pressed into wet clay.','TTS','["A poem","A tally of rations","A royal decree","A prayer"]','B',1,'The professor says the earliest tablets are tallies of grain, beer, and sheep given as rations.',92),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_TALK','Listen to the talk and answer the question.','Professor: Today we look at why the first writing was almost boring. The oldest clay tablets from southern Mesopotamia are not poems or prayers; they are tallies of grain, beer, and sheep handed out as rations. A worker received a fixed measure of barley each day, and the temple had to record who took it, or the storehouse would be emptied without a trace. So the earliest signs are numbers, a picture of a stalk, and a mark naming the person. Only later did the wedge-shaped strokes become flexible enough to say more than a receipt. The lesson is that a technology we now link with literature and law grew out of a plain accounting need: keeping track of what was owed to whom. That is why, when you read a ration list, you are seeing the ancestors of the alphabet at their everyday work, pressed into wet clay.','TTS','["They were lost","They became the alphabet overnight","They later gained signs beyond a receipt","They stopped recording barley"]','C',1,'The talk notes the wedge strokes only later became flexible enough to say more than a receipt.',93),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_TALK','Listen to the talk and answer the question.','Professor: Let us think about how a songbird finds a pond it has never seen. One candidate is a magnetic sense: the bird may read the tilt and strength of the Earth''s field and turn them into a compass reading. Another is a learned map, built from landmarks on the first journey and used on the way back. A third is simple dead reckoning, counting the hours flown and the turns made. Field tests tease these apart. Birds raised away from the migration route still pick a plausible heading, which favours some inherited program, yet birds that have flown the route once adjust far better when the landmarks are shifted. The cautious conclusion is that migration is not one skill but several, layered together, and that the young bird inherits a rough direction it sharpens with experience.','TTS','["One single method all birds share","The inherited compass only","Several abilities layered together","The route a bird learns in a nest"]','C',1,'The talk''s cautious conclusion is that migration combines several abilities, layered together.',94),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_TALK','Listen to the talk and answer the question.','Professor: Let us think about how a songbird finds a pond it has never seen. One candidate is a magnetic sense: the bird may read the tilt and strength of the Earth''s field and turn them into a compass reading. Another is a learned map, built from landmarks on the first journey and used on the way back. A third is simple dead reckoning, counting the hours flown and the turns made. Field tests tease these apart. Birds raised away from the migration route still pick a plausible heading, which favours some inherited program, yet birds that have flown the route once adjust far better when the landmarks are shifted. The cautious conclusion is that migration is not one skill but several, layered together, and that the young bird inherits a rough direction it sharpens with experience.','TTS','["They lost all sense of direction","They flew only at night","They ignored the landmarks","They still chose a plausible heading"]','D',1,'The professor says birds raised away from the route still pick a plausible heading, pointing to an inherited program.',95),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_TALK','Listen to the talk and answer the question.','Professor: Let us think about how a songbird finds a pond it has never seen. One candidate is a magnetic sense: the bird may read the tilt and strength of the Earth''s field and turn them into a compass reading. Another is a learned map, built from landmarks on the first journey and used on the way back. A third is simple dead reckoning, counting the hours flown and the turns made. Field tests tease these apart. Birds raised away from the migration route still pick a plausible heading, which favours some inherited program, yet birds that have flown the route once adjust far better when the landmarks are shifted. The cautious conclusion is that migration is not one skill but several, layered together, and that the young bird inherits a rough direction it sharpens with experience.','TTS','["The first journey alone","The hours flown plus the turns made","The strength of the wind","The number of companions"]','B',1,'The talk describes dead reckoning as counting the hours flown and the turns made.',96),
(@set05_exam_id,'LISTENING','LISTEN_TALK','Listen to the talk and answer the question.','Professor: Let us think about how a songbird finds a pond it has never seen. One candidate is a magnetic sense: the bird may read the tilt and strength of the Earth''s field and turn them into a compass reading. Another is a learned map, built from landmarks on the first journey and used on the way back. A third is simple dead reckoning, counting the hours flown and the turns made. Field tests tease these apart. Birds raised away from the migration route still pick a plausible heading, which favours some inherited program, yet birds that have flown the route once adjust far better when the landmarks are shifted. The cautious conclusion is that migration is not one skill but several, layered together, and that the young bird inherits a rough direction it sharpens with experience.','TTS','["A single skill","An inherited direction refined by experience","A method birds never repeat","A sign learned only in the nest"]','B',1,'The professor concludes the young bird inherits a rough direction and sharpens it with experience.',97);
